ae48cb2a (633 1793265983652 "guenchi" (("4gm4c2jr" . 3240) ("w5vbequy" . 14982)) (put ((kind . section) (title . "landing f365") (src . "import --symbols takes a file it cannot check whole instead of leaving it out\n\nAn import with an editor's symbols refused a file whose cuts could not be\nchecked at all -- no language entry (a .tsx), or a file the scanner cannot\nfollow (JavaScript with JSX) -- and left it out of the import, so the user\nhad to import it again by hand. Such a file is now imported as a plain\nimport would import it, whole, as one block, and listed with its reason in\na new clause, symbols-imported-whole. A refusal that checked a cut and\nfound it wrong (stale symbols, a start inside a body, not at a line start,\nin the prefix, the section's own checks) still leaves the file out, in\nsymbols-refused, since it names a fault the editor's side can fix.\n\n- code-project.sc: capture-import's guard imports the cannot-check kinds\n  whole; the answer gains the clause, only when it is not empty.\n- rpc.sc: the verb's help says so.\n- README: the --symbols section says so, and that the editor extension\n  does not yet name why such a file came in whole.\n- Tests: import-symbols (a .js unscanned, a .tsx without a language entry,\n  a .js with JSX, one answer holding a refused, a whole and a cut file, no\n  clause on a clean import); ecmascript-scan's import rows read the new\n  clause; the unreadable census and the verb registry's description pin;\n  rows-baseline.\n") (parent . root) (ord . 506))))
