f390d389 (653 1793267407913 "guenchi" (("4gm4c2jr" . 3240) ("w5vbequy" . 14982)) (put ((kind . section) (title . "landing f370") (src . "landing: a freeze stays current when nothing that lands has changed\n\nA landing freeze pinned the store's cut, and both its check and the\nlanding commit refused as soon as the cut moved at all, so any record\nwritten after the freeze -- a review's letter, a tag, another writer's\nnote -- forced a new freeze although nothing that would land had changed.\nThe check and the commit now share one judgement: the freeze is current\nwhen no frozen draft is behind, every structural item still applies,\nand no block that a file is made of has changed between the pinned cut\nand now. That comparison walks every holder with a path and every block\nunder it at any depth, comparing each block's hash (its fields, its\nposition, deletion and edges), so a change to any file, a datum library\nincluded, a move into or out of a file, or a reorder is still a moved\nfreeze that names the changed paths. A change to a file the freeze does\nnot hold still refuses: what was gated would not be what lands. The\nstart tag binds the cut that was judged, and a commit between the\njudgement and the tag is still caught. The comparison takes some seconds\non a large store, and it assumes one committer, as before.\n\n- landing-files.sc: file-scope-changes, the comparison.\n- tools/landing-freeze.sc, tools/landing-commit.sc: the shared judgement;\n  a refreeze names (changed-since-pin <path> ...).\n- README: the landing section says so.\n- Tests: drafts-tools (a record after the freeze, a tag, another file's\n  change, a nested block's change, a datum library's change, the commit's\n  start tag); rows-baseline.\n") (parent . root) (ord . 507))))
